<text:p text:style-name="Title">Harbour handbook</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Subtitle">The east quay: rules, figures and notes</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Author">exav project, written for the demo (CC0-1.0)</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Author">1 January 2000</text:p><text:table-of-content text:style-name="Sect1" text:protected="true" text:name="Table of Contents1"><text:table-of-content-source text:outline-level="2"><text:index-title-template text:style-name="Contents_20_Heading">Contents</text:index-title-template></text:table-of-content-source><text:index-body><text:index-title text:style-name="Sect1" text:name="Table of Contents1_Head"><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_Heading">Contents</text:p></text:index-title><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#intro" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">1. Introduction</text:a></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#text" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">2. Text and styles</text:a></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#lists" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">3. Lists</text:a></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#tables" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">4. Tables</text:a></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#pictures" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">5. Pictures and shapes</text:a></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#links" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">6. Links, fields and notes</text:a></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Contents_20_1"><text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#wide" text:style-name="Index_20_Link" text:visited-style-name="Index_20_Link">7. Wide table (landscape)</text:a></text:p></text:index-body></text:table-of-content><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="intro"/>Introduction</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Every berth has a number, a length in metres and a holder. The register is kept on paper and in a table; the two are compared each spring, and the differences are explained in the notes of the harbour master. <text:note text:id="ftn1" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>1</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">The register of 2000 lists sixty berths.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Quotations">“A harbour is a promise that the sea will wait.” </text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Visitors are asked to call the harbour office on channel 9 before they come in, to give the length of their boat and its draught, and to say how many nights they plan to stay.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="text"/>Text and styles</text:h><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Character formatting</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><text:span text:style-name="Strong">Bold</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">italic</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="Underline">underlined</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="Strike">struck through</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="Red">red</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="Highlight">highlighted</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="SmallCaps">small capitals</text:span>, <text:span text:style-name="Big">large</text:span> and <text:span text:style-name="Mono">monospaced</text:span> text; H<text:span text:style-name="Sub">2</text:span>O and 10<text:span text:style-name="Super">3</text:span>; a <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">mixed</text:span> style.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">Paragraph formatting</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Justified">The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. Every berth has a number, a length in metres and a holder. The register is kept on paper and in a table; the two are compared each spring, and the differences are explained in the notes of the harbour master.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Centered">A centred line</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Right">A line aligned to the right</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Indented">An indented paragraph with a left border: Visitors are asked to call the harbour office on channel 9 before they come in, to give the length of their boat and its draught, and to say how many nights they plan to stay.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Code">moor --boat Aurora --length 6.5</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Code">berth 14 free until 06:00</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_2" text:outline-level="2">A section in two columns</text:h><text:section text:style-name="Sect2" text:name="Columns"><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. Every berth has a number, a length in metres and a holder. The register is kept on paper and in a table; the two are compared each spring, and the differences are explained in the notes of the harbour master. Visitors are asked to call the harbour office on channel 9 before they come in, to give the length of their boat and its draught, and to say how many nights they plan to stay. The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell.</text:p></text:section><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="lists"/>Lists</text:h><text:list text:style-name="L1"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Water at every berth</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:list text:style-name="L1"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">cold, from the quay</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">hot, in the shower block</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Electricity</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:list text:style-name="L1"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">16 A at berths 1 to 40</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:list text:style-name="L1"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">with a meter</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">without a meter</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">32 A at the east pontoon</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Wi-Fi on the quay</text:p></text:list-item></text:list><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Numbered, with other numbering styles at each level:</text:p><text:list text:style-name="L2"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Call the office on channel 9</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Give the length and the draught</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:list text:style-name="L2"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">length over all, in metres</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">draught, in metres</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Take the berth you are given</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:list text:style-name="L2"><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">tie up bow first</text:p></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">tie up stern first</text:p></text:list-item></text:list></text:list-item><text:list-item><text:p text:style-name="List_20_Contents">Pay at the office</text:p></text:list-item></text:list><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="tables"/>Tables</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Caption">Table <text:sequence text:ref-name="refTable0" text:name="Table" text:formula="ooow:Table+1" style:num-format="1">1</text:sequence>: berths by length, with merged cells and a repeated header row</text:p><table:table table:name="Table1" table:style-name="Tbl1"><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolA"/><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolB"/><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolC"/><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolD"/><table:table-header-rows><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Th" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Length</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Th" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Berths</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Th" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Let by</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Th" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Fee (EUR)</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row></table:table-header-rows><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">up to 6 m</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="12"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">12</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">week</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="18.0"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">18.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">6 to 8 m</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="18"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">18</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">season</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="24.5"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">24.50</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">8 to 10 m</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="14"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">14</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">season</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="31.0"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">31.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">10 to 12 m</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="9"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">9</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">year</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="42.0"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">42.00</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">over 12 m</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="7"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">7</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">year</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcR" office:value-type="float" office:value="58.5"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">58.50</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcTotal" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents"><text:span text:style-name="Strong">Total</text:span></text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcTotalR" office:value-type="float" office:value="60"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Right">60</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="TcTotal" office:value-type="string" table:number-columns-spanned="2"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents"></text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row></table:table><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"></text:p><table:table table:name="Table2" table:style-name="Tbl1"><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolA"/><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolB"/><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolC"/><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Th" office:value-type="string" table:number-columns-spanned="2"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Heading">Merged across two columns</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string" table:number-rows-spanned="2"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">Merged down two rows</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">a</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">b</text:p></table:table-cell><table:covered-table-cell/></table:table-row><table:table-row><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">c</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">d</text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell table:style-name="Tc" office:value-type="string"><text:p text:style-name="Table_20_Contents">e</text:p></table:table-cell></table:table-row></table:table><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="pictures"/>Pictures and shapes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr1" draw:name="Picture 1" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="8cm" svg:height="4.5cm"><draw:image><office:binary-data></office:binary-data></draw:image><svg:title>A lake at dusk</svg:title><svg:desc>A made-up picture of a lake and a hill at dusk.</svg:desc></draw:frame>The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. Every berth has a number, a length in metres and a holder. The register is kept on paper and in a table; the two are compared each spring, and the differences are explained in the notes of the harbour master. Visitors are asked to call the harbour office on channel 9 before they come in, to give the length of their boat and its draught, and to say how many nights they plan to stay. The east quay was built in three stages. The first stage, a timber jetty of twenty berths, dates from the start of the register; the second doubled it in stone, and the third, the long breakwater, shelters both from the south-west swell. </text:p><text:p text:style-name="Caption">Figure <text:sequence text:ref-name="refFigure0" text:name="Figure" text:formula="ooow:Figure+1" style:num-format="1">1</text:sequence>: a picture that text flows around</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Centered"><draw:frame draw:style-name="fr2" draw:name="Picture 2" text:anchor-type="as-char" svg:width="6cm" svg:height="3.375cm"><draw:image><office:binary-data></office:binary-data></draw:image><svg:title>The second picture</svg:title></draw:frame></text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body"><draw:custom-shape draw:style-name="gr1" draw:name="Callout" text:anchor-type="paragraph" svg:width="6cm" svg:height="2cm" svg:x="2cm" svg:y="0.2cm"><text:p text:style-name="Centered">A shape with text in it</text:p><draw:enhanced-geometry svg:viewBox="0 0 21600 21600" draw:type="round-rectangle" draw:enhanced-path="M 3600 0 X 0 3600 L 0 18000 Y 3600 21600 L 18000 21600 X 21600 18000 L 21600 3600 Y 18000 0 Z N"/></draw:custom-shape>A line of text beside a shape.</text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="links"/>Links, fields and notes</text:h><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">An external link: <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="https://exav.org/" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">exav.org</text:a>. An internal link: <text:a xlink:type="simple" xlink:href="#intro" text:style-name="Internet_20_link" text:visited-style-name="Visited_20_Internet_20_Link">back to the introduction</text:a>. A reference to a bookmark: <text:bookmark-ref text:reference-format="text" text:ref-name="tables">Tables</text:bookmark-ref>.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Fields: this document is titled “<text:title>Harbour handbook</text:title>”, and this line is on page <text:page-number text:select-page="current">1</text:page-number>. A fixed date: <text:date style:data-style-name="N10" text:date-value="2000-01-01" text:fixed="true">01/01/2000</text:date>.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">A comment is attached to this word<office:annotation><dc:creator>exav</dc:creator><dc:date>2000-01-01T00:00:00</dc:date><text:p>A comment: the viewer shows or ignores it.</text:p></office:annotation>. A change that was tracked: <text:change-start text:change-id="ct1"/>this text was inserted<text:change-end text:change-id="ct1"/>, <text:change text:change-id="ct2"/>and some text was deleted before this one.</text:p><text:p text:style-name="Text_20_body">Citations [1] [2]. <text:note text:id="ftn2" text:note-class="footnote"><text:note-citation>2</text:note-citation><text:note-body><text:p text:style-name="Footnote">A second footnote, with <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis">emphasis</text:span>.</text:p></text:note-body></text:note></text:p><text:h text:style-name="Heading_20_1_20_Landscape" text:outline-level="1"><text:bookmark text:name="wide"/>Wide table (landscape)</text:h><table:table table:name="Table3" table:style-name="TblWide"><table:table-column table:style-name="TcolW"/><table:table-column table:style-name="